{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-321225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-2{e}^{x}y+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-321225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-2{e}^{x}y+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=1,\\,b(x)=-2{e}^{x},\\,c(x)={e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{e}^{x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+{e}^{x}=(z+{e}^{x})^{2}-2{e}^{x}(z+{e}^{x})+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & =({e}^{2x}+2{e}^{x}z+{z}^{2})-(2{e}^{2x}+2{e}^{x}z)+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & ={z}^{2}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′} & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-{e}^{x}$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y-{e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}+{e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-321225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "044d6aae10c74302ef290827ceef38c5d188abe20baf62361588b46f84642758"} {"question" "q-321225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-321225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{x+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x-C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2x+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-321225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function ${y}_{0}(x)=-x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{y}^{2}-(2x+1)y-(1+x+{x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=-x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-1$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z-x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-1.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-1=-(z-x)^{2}-(2x+1)(-x+z)-(1+x+{x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-1 & =-({x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xz)-(-2{x}^{2}+2xz-x+z)-(1+x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ {z}^{′}-1 & =-{z}^{2}-z-1 \\\\ {z}^{′}+z & =-{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=1,\\,Q(x)=-1,\\,n=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "044d6aae10c74302ef290827ceef38c5d188abe20baf62361588b46f84642758"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-332991" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function ${y}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)y+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=2x$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{x}^{2}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+2x.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+2x=x(z+{x}^{2})^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)(z+{x}^{2})+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+2x & =x(z+{x}^{2})^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)(z+{x}^{2})+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2) \\\\ {z}^{′}+2x & =x{z}^{2}-2xz+2x \\\\ {z}^{′}+2xz & =x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=2x,\\,Q(x)=x,\\,n=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "044d6aae10c74302ef290827ceef38c5d188abe20baf62361588b46f84642758"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-333616" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=3x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2}y+18{x}^{3}+3\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2}y+18{x}^{3}+3,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=2x,\\,b(x)=-12{x}^{2},\\,c(x)=18{x}^{3}+3.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=3x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=3$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+3x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+3.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+3=2x\\,(z+3x)^{2}-12{x}^{2}(z+3x)+18{x}^{3}+3.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+3 & =2x(9{x}^{2}+6xz+{z}^{2})-12{x}^{2}z-36{x}^{3}+18{x}^{3}+3 \\\\ {z}^{′}+3 & =2x{z}^{2}+3 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-3x$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y-3x & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}+3x \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "044d6aae10c74302ef290827ceef38c5d188abe20baf62361588b46f84642758"} {"question" "q-334117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=3x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y=3x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y=3x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-C}"] ["math" "y=3x-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y=3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=-6x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}+36xy+108{x}^{2}-6\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}+36xy+108{x}^{2}-6,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=3,\\,b(x)=36x,\\,c(x)=108{x}^{2}-6.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=-6x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-6$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z-6x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-6.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-6=3(z-6x)^{2}+36x(z-6x)+108{x}^{2}-6.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-6 & =3(36{x}^{2}-12xz+{z}^{2})+36xz-216{x}^{2}+108{x}^{2}-6 \\\\ {z}^{′}-6 & =3{z}^{2}-6 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =3x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y+6x$ (that is, $y=z-6x$) to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y+6x & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}-6x \\\\  & =-6x-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44f6bd84deadce65bb4e6a3e1401d539aa13899cd"} {"question" "q-334144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "044d6aae10c74302ef290827ceef38c5d188abe20baf62361588b46f84642758"} {"question" "q-334144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1e7501abcdff2990723f3a44